title: Bind relay poll and peek inbox access to a verified owner
---
B111 found that /poll_inbox and /peek_inbox are outer-auth bypasses. Without an Ed25519 header their handlers use caller-supplied node_id/session_id without checking ownership, allowing a party that learns those identifiers to read or drain an inbox.

Acceptance criteria:
- In production require a valid Ed25519 request whose bound alias owns the requested node/session for poll and peek.
- Keep no-auth behavior, if required at all, behind an explicit development-only setting.
- Add negative handler and token-configured HTTP tests for missing proof and proof from a different alias, plus positive owner coverage.
- Confirm heartbeat remains protected by its existing peer-route and ownership check.

Evidence: B111 audit.